+
+Actual commands, from the repository root:
+
+```powershell
+$env:PYTHONPATH='backend'
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 -m pytest backend/tests/test_http_server.py -q --tb=short --basetemp=build/sec09-sec10-fixes-2026-10-24/http-final -p no:cacheprovider --junitxml=docs/evidence/sec09-sec10-fixes-2026-10-24/http.xml
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 -m pytest backend/tests/test_security_fixes.py backend/tests/test_gcp_staging.py backend/tests/test_gcp_update.py backend/tests/test_results_deployment.py -q --tb=short --basetemp=build/sec09-sec10-fixes-2026-10-24/regression-final -p no:cacheprovider --junitxml=docs/evidence/sec09-sec10-fixes-2026-10-24/regression.xml
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/sec0910_linux_http_20261024.py
+.tools/backend-secure-venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 .tools/sec0910_postgres_20261024.py
+```
+
+The Linux and PostgreSQL wrappers use a cached local image for dependencies and mount current backend source read-only. PostgreSQL17 runs on a labelled, owned internal Docker network with tmpfs data and newly generated fixture credentials; cleanup stops only that labelled fixture. The original checker is mounted as a separate control. The Godot-dependent cloud smoke case is explicitly deselected. No player database or cloud credential is involved. Retained copies of the wrappers, the control source, pytest XML/logs and the patch are in the evidence directory.
+
+The first PostgreSQL attempt recorded 53 failures/1 pass before the0065 identifier correction. The second recorded 53 passes/1 failure because the new raw-SQL audit fixture omitted its ORM-generated primary key. The fixture now supplies its ID explicitly; no security invariant was relaxed. Those receipts remain as `postgres-initial.*` and `postgres-second.*`. Existing Starlette deprecation/SQLite expression-index reflection warnings are retained.
+
+## Files and rollout limits
+
+Runtime files: `backend/bmt_backend/http_server.py`, `database_privileges.py`, `object_models.py`, `migrations/versions/0065_packed_objects.py`. Entry points: `backend/Dockerfile`, both Compose files, `backend/deploy/smoke_compose.py`, Google `staging.py`/`update.py`, `scripts/dev.ps1`. Tests: `test_http_server.py`, `test_runtime_privileges.py`, `test_gcp_staging.py`, `test_gcp_update.py`. Backend/deployment/index/status documentation links this report.
+
+The scoped Git patch uses task-start source baselines and documentation baselines captured immediately before this task's insertions, preserving concurrent work. The initial manifest is retained separately. `git apply --reverse --check --ignore-space-change` validates the LF patch against the workspace's mixed Windows line endings; the initial plain check rejected those line-ending differences. No mixed-tree commit is made.
+
+Rollout requires the matching guarded HTTP command and API/worker/private Studio image, the normal owner-run reviewed grants step after migrations, and successful production-mode credential checks. A rollout of the whole current tree must also account for its independently developed0063–0067 features and prerequisites. The earlier cloud release remains separate; this task performs no live migration, GRANT, service update, player mutation, backup/export or deployment. Previous PC backup approval remains outstanding.
+
+No frontend/physics change or visible UI change was made. Device attachment was not checked; no physical-device test, APK, client/owner-process restart, purchase or provider interaction occurred. Real edge/proxy/device/load and deployment-host acceptance remain. Previously accepted SEC01/SEC02/SEC05 policy risks are outside this fix.
